  "evidence_notes": "Emma, 28, diagnosed with Crohn's at 16. Has anxiety disorder and PCOS. History of surgery for fistula. Tried sulfasalazine, mesalamine, 6-MP, and methotrexate with limited success. Started Remicade at 19, lost effectiveness after 3 years. Switched to Humira, worked for 2 years, then lost effectiveness. Currently on Stelara every 8 weeks. Experiences injection anxiety, insurance battles for pre-authorization, fatigue, joint pain, and skin problems. High annual out-of-pocket costs. Lives with parents due to financial strain. Concerned about fertility and pregnancy. Developed osteopenia from steroid use."
